abstract: >-
  A distributed multirobot control system with real-time
  monitoring for an automated industrial painting line. The
  system coordinates two Waveshare RoArm-M2-S spray-painting
  manipulators and a KUKA KR10 R1100-2 pick-and-place robot
  with a conveyor line, using a hybrid architecture: a
  Siemens SIMATIC S7-1500 PLC (TIA Portal V19) for
  deterministic sequencing and safety, and a MATLAB
  supervisory layer for trajectory generation and
  coordination. The conveyor drive is modeled as a
  second-order system and controlled by a MATLAB
  auto-tuned PID verified in Simulink. Communication uses
  PROFINET, OPC UA, TCP/IP (KukaVarProxy), and HTTP/JSON.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - industrial automation
  - PLC
  - SIMATIC S7-1500
  - MATLAB
  - Simulink
  - KUKA
  - RoArm-M2-S
  - PID control
  - multi-robot coordination
  - spray painting
